Issue #46 gadgets, batch 4 leftovers: SWAP and COOK (never committed; saved here so the work is not lost)

Uncommitted edits from a subagent worktree of 2026-11-25 (base 5bba92b, the pre-#71 star-powers branch, kept on GitHub
as backup/focused-mayer-5bba92b). Paths are repo-root relative. Not applied: main's gadget.c has moved on since.

What it adds (engine/native/loader/gadget.c, env.c, superfix_cc.c; super_audit.py classifies and audits the kinds):
- SWAP: swap_weapon_skill with a bounded duration (Jae-Yong `Alternator`: ActiveTicks 100 = 5 s, the replacement
  weapon SkillData, the mode's aura). Uses superfix_cc_swap (Draco's mount swap) and puts the own weapon back after.
  Audit then: Alternator_DamageMode works (3400 damage, AlternatorDamageProjectile, AlternatorDamageAura r1250);
  Alternator_SlowMode was not run.
- COOK: next_attack_change SubType 23 with StatusEffectEnemy (Pearl `Cooker_Poison`): the next volley's victims get the
  status, via a gadget_hit hook in env.c. Audit then: works (5154 damage, healed 600, CookerProjectile x6, damage after
  the hit = "dot", a new super_audit outcome with LATE_AFTER).
- SUMMON is in this diff too, but it already landed in main (#46 batches 3b and 4, 7b454cd): skip those hunks.

To port: apply the SWAP / COOK hunks by hand onto main's gadget.c (`git apply -3` will conflict), record the engine
change in engine/patches/ as AGENTS.md says, rebuild the host, then `python -m gadget_check` and
`python -m super_audit --gadget` for Jae-Yong and Pearl.

